{"chunk_id": "241a0986ac0d", "text": "In the public assembly, the sage Valmiki solemnly testifies to Sita\u2019s absolute purity, swearing the truth of his words on the power of his long ascetic life. Rama acknowledges that he already believed in Sita\u2019s innocence but had banished her out of fear of public opinion. He accepts Lava and Kusha as his sons and seeks reconciliation before the gathered court. Drawn by the gravity of the moment, hosts of gods, sages, and celestial beings assemble to witness Sita\u2019s final vindication. Sita then makes a final oath that she has never thought of any man but Rama. In response, the Earth itself opens: the goddess Dharani rises with a jeweled throne borne by mighty Nagas and receives Sita into her arms. As Sita descends into the Earth, the cosmos trembles and the gods acclaim her supreme virtue.\nBefore gods and sages, Sita proves her fidelity and is received by the Earth goddess, descending into the earth as the assembly watches in awe.\nThemes: chastity and honor, divine vindication, public duty vs personal love, earth goddess, final separation", "vector": [0.02305581048130989, -0.01270034909248352, -0.0025685338769108057, 0.0028819763101637363, -0.021700382232666016, 0.01201585866510868, -0.03030734322965145, -0.0027515164110809565, -0.0211039949208498, -0.022174783051013947, 0.01349327340722084, 0.011033173650503159, 0.010768866166472435, 0.011331368237733841, -0.021131103858351707, -0.0007984311087056994, 0.0367862842977047, -0.004652502480894327, 0.01926061511039734, -0.015072345733642578, -0.007366744801402092, -0.01462505478411913, 0.003696926636621356, 0.013167970813810825, -0.02781335823237896, -0.008634069003164768, 0.03239469975233078, -0.03304530680179596, 0.021551286801695824, -0.013317068107426167, -0.020372064784169197, -0.011534681543707848, -0.011900647543370724, -0.015180779621005058, -0.02329978719353676, 0.00321574998088181, -0.01477415207773447, -0.013974450528621674, 0.006577208638191223, -0.0026312